'<h2>Replacing Carpet on Mercer Island</h2>',

"<p>Mercer Island carpet skews older than the eastside average &mdash; a lot of the island's mid-century and 1980s houses still carry carpet from a remodel two owners "
"ago, and the question we get in those living rooms is rarely whether it is time but how it did not come up sooner. The island pattern: bedrooms and rec rooms getting "
"honest family wear, daylight basements with the moisture question that every below-grade room on the lake has to answer, and a steady stream of pre-listing "
"refreshes where new carpet in the bedrooms is the cheapest line item in the whole staging budget. The mobile showroom handles all of it in one visit &mdash; "
"twenty-plus full-size samples and all three pad grades in your own light, every room and stair measured, tear-out and haul-away in the written price you get before "
"we leave. Details on the <a href=\"/city-of-mercer-island/carpet-installation-in-mercer-island-wa\">Mercer Island carpet installation page</a>.</p>",

faq('Replacing Carpet: What Homeowners Ask Us', [
 ('How do I know when carpet needs to be replaced?',
  'Five signs: matting that will not fluff back up after cleaning, odor that returns after professional extraction, visible backing or failing seams, a pad that has gone crunchy or flat underfoot, and age — around fifteen-plus years — where deep cleans no longer hold. If your complaint is not on that list, there is a decent chance the fix is cheaper than a new floor.'),
 ('How long does carpet usually last?',
  'Quality carpet over a good pad runs ten to fifteen years in normal family use; builder-grade over cheap pad can be visibly done in five to seven. The room matters as much as the product — bedroom carpet lives far longer than family-room carpet — and the pad quietly decides more of the lifespan than the carpet label does.'),
 ('My carpet looks flat and dirty in the traffic lanes. Is it worn out?',
  'Run the fluff test: rub the matted area briskly against the pile. Fibers that stand back up and stay up are dirty, not dead — book a hot-water extraction and be pleasantly surprised. Fibers that stay flat or slump back within the hour have lost their twist, and no cleaning brings that back. That is the difference between a cleaning bill and a new floor.'),
 ('Why does my carpet still smell after professional cleaning?',
  'Because the smell is not in the carpet. Odor that survives extraction lives in the pad or subfloor, where surface cleaning cannot reach — classic with old pet accidents and moisture. The fix is replacement: old carpet and pad out, subfloor inspected and sealed if needed, and a moisture-barrier pad under the new carpet so the story does not repeat.'),
 ('Should I restretch my carpet or replace it?',
  'If the problem is ripples, waves or a wrinkle at the doorway and the carpet itself is healthy, restretch — it costs a fraction of replacement and the floor is flat by lunch. Replace when the fibers are matted flat, the backing shows, or wrinkles return after a proper restretch, which means the pad underneath has collapsed. We quote whichever one your floor actually needs.'),
 ('Is it worth replacing carpet before selling a house?',
  'Usually, yes — old carpet photographs badly and invites lowball mental math from every buyer who walks in, while fresh neutral carpet in bedrooms is one of the cheapest per-dollar upgrades in a listing. From $1.49 per square foot installed and done in a day, it routinely returns more than it costs in offer strength. Your agent will say the same thing.'),
 ('Do you handle tearing out and disposing of the old carpet?',
  'Yes — tear-out of the old carpet, pad, staples and tack strip, plus haul-away and disposal, is part of the job and part of the written price. You do not need to rent a truck or fight a carpet roll down the stairs. If you want to pull it yourself to save a line item, we will tell you honestly what that saves and how to do it safely.'),
 ('Can you check whether my carpet is worth saving before I commit to anything?',
  'That is what the estimate is for. We run the fluff test, check the pad, look for the restretch-versus-replace tells, and tell you plainly if a cleaning or a stretch is the better move — it costs us a sale now and earns us the next three referrals. If it is time, the samples and pad grades are already in the van, and the written price arrives the same visit.'),
]),

